Subject: [PATCH 09536/11362] [outer-loop] Wire self-supervision: sentinel per
 iteration, ledger at close
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

REQ-CONDUCTOR-SENTINEL-3 / REQ-OPS-AUDIT-LEDGER-1 wiring. research_step
runs the sentinel through _run_audit_with_receipt with the sentinel's
always-rewritten state file as the receipt; milestone close runs the
findings ledger right after the claim audit, with its own separate
receipt so a fresh sentinel scan cannot mask a crashed ledger run. The
orphan-cleanup janitor also invokes the sentinel ABOVE its
conductor-liveness early-exit, covering outer-loop-launched runs (the
2026-08-22 incident class). E2E: real runs against the live box —
clean sentinel scan, and the ledger ingested today's two real
CLAIM_OVERSTATED findings (exp6478, exp6497) as OPEN rows.

Wiring mutation proven: sentinel call removed -> wiring test RED,
restored -> 4 GREEN. Conductor picks the change up at its next restart.

